Subject: [PATCH] validation: rearm producer after current buffer replacement

Project-local integration correction for the pinned validation desktop after
0001-0004. This is not represented as a new upstream commit.

An ordinary resize can replace all PipeWire buffers while the stream remains
STREAMING. The frame-lifetime backport correctly cancels the frame attached
to the removed current buffer, but that also removes the frame-ready callback
which drives the next graph iteration. No state transition restarts the graph.

Reuse the existing starvation retry from upstream commit
d24d6a1b726352eb2645c38416b76e214e54a7c0 by Scott Leggett
<scott@sl.id.au>: arm it only when replacement removes the current buffer of
a live stream. Its timer triggers after the native removal callback returns,
retries at the negotiated rate until a buffer is available, and is disarmed by
the existing successful dequeue, PAUSED and teardown paths. Do not directly
re-enter capture while PipeWire is replacing the buffer array.

Upstream retry source: src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c, Git blob
69176df81d2e50f1f50359a410b3334de59c79bb at the commit above.
Frame cancellation source: 5724a432fc95690aef19e55e62178d71b60d0cbb,
already attributed in 0002/upstream.json.
Base: e1d5d16f0e064a0b788c5d70c11461b15ee7a4af plus patches 0001-0004.
License: MIT, matching the retained upstream license and project license.

This adds no pixels or new scheduling loop, changes no client assertion or
deadline, and applies only to the owned validation producer. Positive resize
and refresh behavior must still pass their real compositor probes.

--- a/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c
+++ b/src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@
 
 #define DAMAGE_REGION_COUNT 16
 
+static void pwr_arm_process_retry(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast);
 static void pwr_disarm_process_retry(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast);
 
 static struct spa_pod *build_buffer(struct spa_pod_builder *b, uint32_t blocks, uint32_t size,
@@ -597,6 +598,12 @@
 		cast->current_frame.pw_buffer = NULL;
 		cast->current_frame.xdpw_buffer = NULL;
 		xdpw_wlr_frame_cancel(cast);
+		if (!cast->destroy_pending && cast->pwr_stream_state) {
+			// Cancelling the frame also removes its driver trigger. Retry after
+			// PipeWire finishes replacing buffers, using the existing timer.
+			logprint(DEBUG, "pipewire: current buffer removed while streaming, retrying process");
+			pwr_arm_process_retry(cast);
+		}
 	}
 	for (uint32_t plane = 0; plane < buffer->buffer->n_datas; plane++) {
 		buffer->buffer->datas[plane].fd = -1;
